--- from code review, client branch (see CLAUDE-review.md STATUS section) ---
Blocking items are all fixed; these are what's left. Pinned for now.

6.  README.md:25 still claims the client "has no third-party runtime dependency"
    It imports httpx, which is a required dep in pyproject.toml. Just false now.

7.  Edge attributes: zero test coverage AND no read path
    Nothing in get_neighbors, no HTTP route, nothing in the query engine reads them.
    They are write-only state. The _ADD_EDGE_LUA SET/DEL branch is never exercised,
    including "re-add without attributes clears the old ones".
    Decision first (add a reader, or drop the parameter), then tests.

8.  query_engine._collect_nodes computes degree it throws away
    Calls graph.get_node, which always computes degree, then discards it unless
    degrees was requested. A stage asking only for attributes pays the full
    EXISTS + SMEMBERS + ZCARD-per-edge-type cost for nothing. Cheapest perf win.

9.  Engine validates its own output on every request (query_engine.py:53)
    Builds a QueryResult, to_dict()s it, re-parses it through load_query_response,
    to_dict()s it again. Re-isinstance-checks every node id on the hot path, on data
    it just built. Drop it or put it behind a debug flag.

10. _topological_stage_levels builds the dependency graph twice
    Calls topological_stage_names() for its cycle check, discards the result, then
    rebuilds identical indegree/dependents dicts and re-runs Kahn's. One function
    returning levels removes ~20 lines and half the work.

11. Client polish (all in src/client.py)
    - :309 arity check is unreachable, every caller passes a literal 2-tuple
    - the trailing `.query` needed to run a chain (see tests/test_client.py:204) --
      put execute()/to_dict() on Stage, or return self.query from a terminal method
    - the four set methods aren't keyword-only, unlike follow_edges
    - NutmegQuery.execute reaches into client._request

12. QueryResult.get_nodes raises bare KeyError, get_scores returns {}
    Pick one. KeyError naming the available stages is friendlier for both.

13. Engine does set math in Python, not in Redis
    ZUNIONSTORE/ZINTERSTORE/SDIFF never appear -- _execute_set_op materializes every
    stage as a full Python list in server memory. Defensible v1 (results must be
    ordered anyway) but the README's "optimized for set operations" describes the
    zset storage layer, not the engine. Fix the engine or soften the README.

14. _execute_follow fan-out is uncapped and unpipelined
    One get_neighbors per source node concurrently, each awaiting one zrangebyscore
    per edge type sequentially. A follow over 10k nodes is 10k concurrent round trips,
    no pipelining, no semaphore. First thing to fall over on real data.
    Related: no bound on plan size at /queries/execute, so one posted plan can
    saturate the connection pool.

15. Remaining query_wire validation rules with no test
    tests/test_query_wire.py covers most of them now. Still unexercised: duplicate
    stage names, zero/two start stages, set kinds with one or three sources,
    non-follow stages carrying edge_type or score bounds, non-boolean flags.
    Cheap rows to add to the parametrize table that already exists.

16. Two test-naming/coverage nits
    - test_set_operations_handle_overlapping_and_empty_inputs doesn't test overlapping
      inputs (left={alice,bob,cara}, right={erin} -- disjoint). The empty half is real;
      rename to ..._handle_empty_results.
    - symmetric_difference has both extremes tested (disjoint -> everything, identical
      -> []) but not partial overlap, the only case exercising exclusion AND ordering
      together, and the shape real queries take.
